  "response_text": "The stack pool is a reserved block of memory from which each thread gets its own stack space. In future labs, when multiple threads are introduced, the kernel will divide this pool into equally sized stacks, one per thread. Each new thread is allocated a section of this pool using a stack allocator, which tracks used and remaining space. This enables the OS to support multiple independent execution contexts without their stacks overlapping, which is critical for stability and proper thread switching.\\n",
